  "goodToKnow": "Der Alkoholiker (die Alkoholikerin) is an alcoholic: ein trockener Alkoholiker is a recovering alcoholic who no longer drinks. Germany has an estimated 1.6 million people with alcohol dependency, and alcohol is cheap and widely accepted socially; beer and wine can be bought from age 16. Help is available through the Anonyme Alkoholiker and addiction counselling services (Suchtberatung). Plural: die Alkoholiker."
